	affiliations = {Universidad Nacional de Córdoba, Departamento de Computación, Cordoba, Argentina},
	abstract = {The mass use of artificial intelligence tools is a reality that is currently going through and seems to trigger an important paradigm shift in work and educational fields. This article exposes the impact generated by one of these new artificial intelligence tools, ChatGPT, in teaching the basic concepts of programming. To achieve this goal, the behavior of this technology is analyzed in the resolution of evaluations of an introductory subject to programming in C++ of the Facultad de Ciencias Exactas, Física y Naturales de la Universidad Nacional de Córdoba, Argentina. With this analysis, it is revealed that ChatGPT is capable of solving the evaluative exercises with an effectiveness percentage of 97%, therefore, a student without the necessary knowledge can pass an exam. From this, it can be concluded that the reliability of current evaluation methods is in jeopardy. In addition, it is possible to infer that the misuse of this technology by students in the early stages of learning has a negative impact on their training. On the other hand, the potential for validation and tutoring provided by this tool is highlighted when it is used honestly. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
