	affiliations = {Government Engineering College, Department of Computer Science and Engineering, Idukki, India},
	abstract = {Programming with natural language is an area of research with different kinds of applications including introductory programming, robotics, etc. Factors like meaning preservation, ambiguity handling, etc, have to be considered while writing programs in natural language. Natural language programming is evolved over the past years through various developments. Here we introduce a system that can convert sentences written in natural language (we considered English as an example) to python statements. The main feature of our system is that the English sentences need not be grammatically correct. We named our system as Artificial Level Language (ALL) as it can be thought of as a new level, above the high-level language, in the programming language hierarchy. The main component of ALL is a tranSMachine comprised of two parts namely tranScripter and transCompiler. The tranScripter introduced here is named as JAVS-tranScripter which includes a set of protocols that are expected to be improved in the future. ALL take English statements as input and it generates Python code in the background to carry out the instructions and outputs the results. © 2023 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
